---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Legal
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How boothe.io handles your data: it mostly doesn't. Standard hosting logs only, no accounts, no tracking."
	label="privacy"
	updated="2026-09-18"
>
	<p>
		boothe.io is the personal website of Eric Boothe: a blog, a portfolio, and a
		few in-browser demos. This policy explains what the site does and doesn't
		collect. The short version is that it collects almost nothing.
	</p>

	<h2>What this site collects</h2>
	<p>
		The site has no accounts, no sign-up, no comments, no newsletter, and no
		contact forms. It does not set advertising or analytics cookies and does not
		use third-party analytics or tracking pixels.
	</p>
	<p>
		The only data associated with your visit is the standard information any web
		server receives when it serves a page:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>your IP address,</li>
		<li>the URL you requested and the referring page, if any,</li>
		<li>your browser's user-agent string and request headers,</li>
		<li>the date and time of the request.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		This information is processed by the hosting provider (Cloudflare) as part
		of serving the site, protecting it from abuse, and producing aggregate
		traffic statistics. I do not combine it with any other data or use it to
		identify individual visitors.
	</p>

	<h2>Local storage on your device</h2>
	<p>
		The site remembers a few preferences in your own browser so that pages look
		the same from one visit to the next, for example your light/dark theme choice
		and the state of in-browser demos. That data is stored with
		<code>localStorage</code> and a first-party <code>theme</code> cookie. It
		never leaves your device and you can clear it at any time through your
		browser settings.
	</p>

	<h2>Third-party services</h2>
	<p>
		Pages load web fonts from Google Fonts, which means your browser sends a
		request (including your IP address) to Google when a page loads. Google's
		handling of those requests is described in the
		<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
		Links to external sites (GitHub, portfolio companies, and so on) are
		governed by those sites' own policies.
	</p>

	<h2>OAuth applications</h2>
	<p>
		I also build small Google OAuth applications for my own personal automation.
		They access only my own Google account data and are not intended for other
		users. See the <a href="/legal/app-terms">App Terms</a> for details. Any data
		those applications handle is treated according to this policy: it is not
		sold, shared, or used for advertising.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>
		This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly
		collect personal information from anyone.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with
		a new "last updated" date.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this policy can be sent to
		<a href="mailto:ericboothe@gmail.com">ericboothe@gmail.com</a>.
	</p>
</Legal>
